ty"}]},{"type":"h","text":"International Application Pack"},{"type":"p","text":"Prepare:"},{"type":"h","text":"Academic"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"B.Tech degree"},{"text":"Transcripts"},{"text":"CV"},{"text":"SOP"},{"text":"Recommendations"},{"text":"English-language test where required"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Regulatory portfolio"},{"type":"p","text":"Include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Device classification analysis"},{"text":"ISO 14971 risk assessment"},{"text":"Technical file"},{"text":"Regulatory gap assessment"},{"text":"Standards matrix"},{"text":"Global regulatory comparison"},{"text":"Regulatory internship"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This portfolio can demonstrate that the student understands the actual workflow of regulatory affairs."}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A typical pathway:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Tech Biomedical Engineering","Regulatory / QA Intern","Regulatory Affairs Associate","Regulatory Affairs Specialist","Senior Regulatory Affairs Specialist","Regulatory Submission Lead","Regulatory Affairs Manager","Senior Regulatory Manager","Global Regulatory Affairs Director"]},{"type":"h","text":"Alternative QA/RA pathway"},{"type":"flow","items":["Regulatory Associate","QA/RA Specialist","Quality & Regulatory Manager","Head of Quality & Regulatory","Site / Global Quality Leader"]},{"type":"h","text":"PhD / Research Directions"},{"type":"p","text":"A PhD is generally not necessary for Regulatory Affairs."},{"type":"p","text":"It becomes relevant for research, advanced medical-device development or academic careers."},{"type":"p","text":"Potential areas:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI/ML medical-device regulation"},{"text":"Digital health regulation"},{"text":"SaMD"},{"text":"AI-enabled medical devices"},{"text":"Medical-device cybersecurity"},{"text":"Clinical evidence"},{"text":"Combination products"},{"text":"Biomaterials regulation"},{"text":"Implantable-device safety"},{"te